# 28. Tasks

Tasks can be:

- linked to client;
- linked to appointment;
- linked to job;
- linked to project;
- linked to invoice;
- independent.

Fields:

- title;
- assignee;
- due date;
- priority;
- status;
- reminder.

AI can create tasks from conversations.

---

# 29. Waiting List

Client can specify:

- service;
- preferred staff;
- earliest date;
- latest date;
- day preferences;
- time range.

When a matching slot opens:

1. system finds compatible waiting-list entries;
2. owner can approve outreach, or automation can run according to settings;
3. client receives offer;
4. first confirmed response may reserve slot.

---

# 30. No-Show Prevention

Configurable automation:

```text
Booking created
→ confirmation message

24h before
→ reminder

2h before
→ reminder

No confirmation
→ flag for admin
```

Optional:

- deposit;
- stored payment provider token;
- cancellation window;
- no-show label.

---

# 31. Recurring Services

Support recurring appointments/jobs.

Examples:

- weekly cleaning;
- biweekly lesson;
- monthly website maintenance;
- six-month vehicle service reminder.

Recurrence patterns:

- daily;
- weekly;
- monthly;
- custom interval.

---

# 32. Follow-Up Automation

After completed service:

```text
+2 hours
→ thank-you message

+1 day
→ review request

+30 days
→ rebooking reminder
```

Rules configurable per service.

---

# 33. Client Portal

Client can view:

- upcoming appointments;
- previous appointments;
- jobs;
- quotes;
- invoices;
- payments;
- files;
- forms;
- messages.

Client can:

- confirm;
- reschedule if allowed;
- cancel if allowed;
- accept quote;
- pay invoice;
- upload file;
- complete form;
- request another service.

